WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.880
A street in Verona.

2
00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:04.200
Two servants pass two others.

3
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.230
One of them bites his thumb.

4
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.490
"Do you bite your thumb at us, sir?"

5
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.770
And words lead to swords.

6
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.290
A third man steps in, then a fourth.

7
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:17.020
Citizens pile in, then the
two old heads of the families,

8
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.570
waving swords far too big for them.

9
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:24.750
The Prince counts "Three civil
brawls, bred of an airy word."

10
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.320
What started the feud?

11
00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.600
Nobody says.

12
00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.800
So why do they keep fighting?

13
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.720
In this mission, you'll
watch the first brawl grow,

14
00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:34.370
frame by frame.

15
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:39.680
You'll open a fencing manual from 1595,
and ask what it says about quarrels.

16
00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:43.710
And you'll follow the one scene
where the whole play turns.

17
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.480
Your mission: work out why
everyone keeps fighting.
